## Simple logic — no overengineering

### Providers

State holders only. No screen-specific or field-specific methods on notifiers.

- `build()` → empty/default instance
- One generic `update` that merges state (`copyWith` or assign)
- One `clear` / reset method
- UI reads current state, runs its own logic, passes the result to `update`

```dart
void update(StateModel next) {
  state = state.copyWith(
    search: next.search,
    areaId: next.areaId,
  );
}

void clear() => state = const StateModel();
```

```dart
final current = ref.read(filterProvider);
ref.read(filterProvider.notifier).update(
  current.copyWith(search: query),
);
```

### Temp providers (`lib/data/providers/temp/`)

Use when widgets need shared field state instead of constructor props.

- One notifier per reusable field group (search query, dialog draft text, form fields, etc.)
- `Notifier` for sync UI state; `AsyncNotifier` only when the temp holder itself loads async data
- Freezed state model when multiple fields; single `String`/`bool` when one field
- Export from `temp.dart`
- If another screen needs the same fields, reuse the same temp provider — do not duplicate

```dart
@riverpod
class SearchFilterTemp extends _$SearchFilterTemp {
  @override
  SearchFilterState build() => const SearchFilterState();

  void update(SearchFilterState next) => state = next;

  void clear() => state = const SearchFilterState();
}
```

Screen watches the temp provider; shared widgets read/write through the provider. No props drilling.

### Props between widgets

Do not pass data or callbacks through widget constructors unless there is no practical alternative (e.g. `ListView` item index, router `extra`, platform callback).

Prefer:

1. Temp provider in `lib/data/providers/temp/`
2. Feature-scoped Riverpod provider in `lib/data/providers/`
3. `ShadTheme.of(context)` / `Theme.of(context)` for visuals

Never pass styling, labels, or draft values down a widget tree when a provider can hold them.

### Screens

One file, one screen widget. Private helpers stay in that file.

- Watch providers for data and loading
- Local draft vs server original — submit disabled until they differ
- Loading: dim content + centered spinner from provider `isLoading`
- Submit: `try/catch` → user feedback → `pop()` on success
- Change only what was asked; do not touch unrelated files

## Shared widgets (`lib/ui/shared/widgets/`)

All reusable UI primitives live here. One component type = one file. Multiple named constructors or factory constructors for variants — not separate files per variant.

| File (example) | Wraps shadcn | Constructors (examples) |
|---|---|---|
| `app_button.dart` | `ShadButton` | `AppButton.primary`, `AppButton.destructive`, `AppButton.ghost` |
| `app_text_field.dart` | `ShadInput` / `ShadInputFormField` | `AppTextField.standard`, `AppTextField.search`, `AppTextField.password` |
| `app_dialog.dart` | `ShadDialog` | `AppDialog.confirm`, `AppDialog.alert`, `AppDialog.sheet` |
| `app_card.dart` | `ShadCard` | `AppCard.standard`, `AppCard.interactive`, `AppCard.stat` |

Rules for shared widgets:

- Use shadcn_ui components inside — not raw `TextField`, `ElevatedButton`, `AlertDialog`
- Read field state from temp providers; do not accept `value` / `onChanged` props unless the widget is a pure layout shell with zero state
- Use `ShadTheme.of(context)` for colors and `ShadTheme.of(context).textTheme` for typography
- Export each file from `shared/widgets/widgets.dart`
- Before using a shadcn component API, read its page on [mariuti.com/flutter-shadcn-ui](https://mariuti.com/flutter-shadcn-ui/)

```dart
class AppTextField extends ConsumerWidget {
  const AppTextField._({
    required this.tempProvider,
    required this.field,
    this.placeholder,
    super.key,
  });

  factory AppTextField.search() => AppTextField._(
    tempProvider: searchFilterTempProvider,
    field: SearchField.query,
  );
}
```

## UI library — shadcn_ui

Install: `flutter pub add shadcn_ui`

App shell: `ShadApp.custom` + `MaterialApp` + `ShadAppBuilder` so Material, Riverpod, and EasyLocalization coexist. See [Getting started](https://mariuti.com/flutter-shadcn-ui/).

```dart
return ShadApp.custom(
  themeMode: themeMode,
  darkTheme: ThemeSelector.shadDark,
  lightTheme: ThemeSelector.shadLight,
  appBuilder: (context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      theme: Theme.of(context),
      localizationsDelegates: const [
        GlobalShadLocalizations.delegate,
        GlobalMaterialLocalizations.delegate,
        GlobalCupertinoLocalizations.delegate,
        GlobalWidgetsLocalizations.delegate,
      ],
      builder: (context, child) => ShadAppBuilder(child: child!),
      home: home,
    );
  },
);
```

Prefer shadcn components everywhere in UI code: `ShadButton`, `ShadInput`, `ShadCard`, `ShadDialog`, `ShadSelect`, `ShadToast` / Sonner, `ShadTabs`, etc. Lucide icons via exported `LucideIcons` from shadcn_ui.

Do not use Shabakat `AppColors`, gold palette, or `ControlsThemes` styling. Those files are legacy placeholders until migrated.

## Theming — Matrix hacker

Visual direction: dark terminal aesthetic — near-black background, matrix neon green primary, muted green-gray surfaces, monospace typography, subtle green glow on focus/active primary elements.

Single assembly point: `lib/core/themes/theme_selector.dart` builds `ShadThemeData` for light and dark. Supporting tokens only in:

- `lib/core/themes/app_colors.dart` — matrix palette constants (not Shabakat gold)
- `lib/core/themes/app_gradients.dart` — gradients from `AppColors` only
- `lib/core/themes/theme_mode_provider.dart` — persisted theme mode

Base shadcn scheme: start from `ShadGreenColorScheme.dark()` / `.light()` or extend `ShadColorScheme` with matrix values. Override via `ShadThemeData(colorScheme: …)` per [Theme Data](https://mariuti.com/flutter-shadcn-ui/theme-data/).

Matrix palette targets:

| Role | Dark | Light |
|---|---|---|
| background | `#020804` | `#0A0F0A` |
| foreground | `#E8FFE8` | `#0D1F0D` |
| primary | `#00FF41` | `#00C832` |
| primary foreground | `#001A08` | `#F0FFF0` |
| surface / card | `#041208` | `#F4FFF4` |
| muted foreground | `#5C8A5C` | `#4A6B4A` |
| border | `#0F3D1F` | `#C8E6C8` |
| destructive | `#FF4444` | `#DC2626` |

Typography: monospace family (e.g. JetBrains Mono via `google_fonts` or bundled font) on `ShadThemeData.textTheme`.

In widgets:

- `ShadTheme.of(context).colorScheme` for colors — never `Colors.xxx`, never hardcoded `Color(0x…)` in UI files
- `ShadTheme.of(context).textTheme` for text — never raw `TextStyle` in widgets
- `Theme.of(context)` only for Material bridges shadcn already maps
- No `isDarkMode` booleans — use `Theme.of(context).brightness` or shadcn scheme

Component-level overrides: `ShadThemeData` properties (`primaryButtonTheme`, etc.) in `ThemeSelector`, not per-widget color props.

## Layout

- Spacing, padding, breakpoints → `AppSizes` on `BuildContext` (`context.paddingMedium`, `context.borderRadiusLarge`, etc.). No magic numbers in widgets.
- Split large widgets into private classes (`_Header`, `_ActionButton`) instead of deep nesting.
- `const` constructors where possible.

## New UI checklist

1. shadcn component exists? → use it or wrap it in `lib/ui/shared/widgets/`
2. Same fields in multiple places? → temp provider in `lib/data/providers/temp/`
3. New shared variant? → add constructor to existing shared widget file
4. Theme tweak? → `ThemeSelector` / `ShadThemeData`, not inline styles
5. shadcn API unclear? → read [mariuti.com/flutter-shadcn-ui](https://mariuti.com/flutter-shadcn-ui/) first
